{
  "_README": [
    "Slots for the MANY-SLOT probe (Plan 2) and the token tags of the PER-TOKEN MAP (Plan 1).",
    "Read by scripts/cross_route.py --probes (Plan 2, slurm/12_many_slots.sbatch) and by",
    "plots/plot_per_token_map.py (Plan 1 tagging). Annotated 2026-10-10 BEFORE either job ran;",
    "commit this file before sbatch so the slot list and its coding predate the results.",
    "",
    "WHY. Stage 5's 'names resist, occupations collapse' rests on 4 resisting slots, and the",
    "candidate explanations are tangled: names are proper nouns AND appear in 20 answers AND",
    "are copyable from 19 questions. Tolstoi (1 answer, resists) vs Goncourt (1 answer,",
    "collapses) is n=1 vs n=1. This file codes every fact-bearing span in the 40 answers so",
    "slot type, repetition and copyability can be compared within strata.",
    "",
    "RULES. `target` occurs EXACTLY ONCE in that fact's French answer (standalone forget01_fr,",
    "pass 2 -- the trained wording); cross_route.py skips the slot otherwise. Stage 5's 14",
    "slots are kept under their original ids, so this run re-measures them (a reproduction",
    "check against results/cross_route.json, up to ~3.8pp scoring noise).",
    "",
    "FIELDS.",
    "  type  coarse, as Stage 5: common (must be translated) / proper (carried as-is) / number",
    "  kind  fine: name, place, award, title, occupation, genre, origin, identity, style,",
    "        theme, date",
    "  cue_in_question  hand judgement: the question already names this slot or an obvious",
    "        variant of it (Al-Koweit -> Koweit, 'Le Paradis des voleurs' -> Thieves'",
    "        Paradise), so the cell measures COPYING, not recall. cross_route.py's automatic",
    "        leak check catches exact words only and SKIPS those cells; this flag also covers",
    "        the variants it misses. Copyable slots are kept on purpose: in Plan 1 they are",
    "        the control for the retain-protects-copying hypothesis (do copied ATTRIBUTES",
    "        resist the way copied NAMES do?).",
    "  Repetition (how many forget answers carry the slot) is NOT hand-coded -- the analysis",
    "  scripts count it from the data, so it cannot drift from the text.",
    "",
    "LEFT OUT. Fact 1 (garbled translation 'Athar ... S. Mal.'). Facts 14, 38 (no slot that",
    "is both a fact and absent from its question). Vague descriptive answers contribute at",
    "most one style/theme slot each; those kinds are reported separately, never pooled with",
    "occupations."
  ],
